WEBVTT

00:08:58.134 --> 00:09:00.303
so you've got to have enough data

00:09:00.327 --> 00:09:03.871
to train the translation
pairs of languages.

00:09:03.895 --> 00:09:06.789
So if you go to a country

00:09:06.813 --> 00:09:10.387
in which the language is spoken
only by a few thousand people,

00:09:10.411 --> 00:09:12.328
then you probably don't have the data.

00:09:12.352 --> 00:09:16.379
So you've still got to go
to one of the more popular languages

00:09:16.403 --> 00:09:18.236
or more populous countries

00:09:18.260 --> 00:09:19.442
for this to work well.

00:09:20.617 --> 00:09:22.768
CA: It seems to me
that this is just one area

00:09:22.792 --> 00:09:25.434
where people haven't even begun
to really follow through

00:09:25.458 --> 00:09:26.831
on the implications of that.

00:09:26.855 --> 00:09:29.006
People hear about this maybe,

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:31.340
but clearly don't believe it yet,